  "view": "top orthographic unless a cell says otherwise; default zoom 440 px per metre (merge distance 3 px of world = 0.0068255 m); wheel zoom x2^(1/4) per step",
  "focus_plane_y": 1.0,
  "click_quantum": "a clicked position is rounded to a zoom-dependent quantum: 0.005 m at 440 px/m, 0.002 at 622, 0.01 at 110 (the earlier placement fixture's 0.01 at 440 is a coincidence of its pixels)",
  "scene_geometry": "pre-existing vertices/triangles are created in the SAME foreground mesh before the tool activates (they stand for committed geometry); new points come only from real pointer clicks/drags and panel typing"
 },
 "law": "lines: n-1 two-point polygons [i,i+1] in click order, close adds [n-1,0]; mirrored segments keep the order [m(a),m(b)] with mirror vertices appended in click order. vertices: free vertices, no polygons. subdiv: one polygon of the subdivision kind (its ring faces the camera like a plain polygon). Select-new on: the new vertices and new edges are selected in every selection mode, the new polygon only in polygon mode; the prior selection is kept; the mode does not change. Select-new off: nothing new is selected and the prior selection is untouched.",
